# LF everywhere, in the working tree too.
#
# Git already stores these blobs with LF; the problem is the checkout. On
# Windows `core.autocrlf=true` is the default, so the working tree comes back
# CRLF -- and the release tooling runs against the working tree, from WSL:
#
#   deploy/bump-version.sh reads the version out of Cargo.toml with awk. The
#   section header arrives as `[workspace.package]\r`, never equals
#   `[workspace.package]`, and the release stops at "no version field found".
#   In Cargo.lock the same stray \r makes the package-name match miss, which is
#   worse -- nothing errors, the lockfile simply keeps the old version.
#
# The parent repo settled this the same way on 2026-07-31, for the same reason:
# pin the whole tree rather than patch one parser at a time. text=auto leaves
# binaries alone.
* text=auto eol=lf
